  ["The Loomis Chaffee School", "Windsor, CT", "$77,340 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://www.loomischaffee.org/admission"],
  ["The Taft School", "Watertown, CT", "$81,400 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://www.taftschool.org/admission"],
  ["Middlesex School", "Concord, MA", "$82,575 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://www.mxschool.edu/admissions"],
  ["Milton Academy", "Milton, MA", "$79,900 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://www.milton.edu/admission"],
  ["Cate School", "Carpinteria, CA", "$87,340 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://www.cate.org/admission/"],
  ["St. Andrew's School", "Middletown, DE", "$78,500 (2026–2027, 100% boarding)", "January 15", "https://www.standrews-de.org/admission"],
  ["The Peddie School", "Hightstown, NJ", "$81,000 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://peddie.org/admission/"],
  ["Concord Academy", "Concord, MA", "$84,410 (2026–2027)", "January 15", "https://concordacademy.org/admissions/"]
].map(r => r.join("\t")).join("\n");

const summarySection = [
  "",
  "SUMMARY & ANALYSIS",
  "Tuition Range\tAnnual boarding tuition across these top schools ranges from $62,740 (Groton School, which leads in cost-containment via GRAIN) to $87,340 (Cate School in CA), with most schools clustering between $77,000 and $82,000. All of these schools maintain significant endowments and generous need-based financial aid (several provide 100% free tuition for families under $150k income).",
  "Geographic Concentration\tSchools are concentrated overwhelmingly in the Northeast: Massachusetts (6), Connecticut (4), New Hampshire (2), and New Jersey (2), with St. Andrew's representing Delaware and Cate School representing California.",
  "",
  "PRACTICAL RECOMMENDATIONS & STARTING POINTS",
  "1. Flagship Titans\tPhillips Exeter Academy (NH) and Phillips Academy Andover (MA): Unmatched academic offerings, collegiate resources, pure Harkness discussion method, need-blind admissions, and global prestige.",
  "2. 100% Boarding Communities\tSt. Paul's School (NH) and St. Andrew's School (DE): Rare 100% residential boarding environments where all students and faculty reside on campus, creating tight-knit communities.",
  "3. Best Value & Warmth\tGroton School (MA): Exceptional Ivy/top-college placement, small supportive community (~380 students), and the lowest tuition among top-tier peers ($62,740).",
  "4. West Coast Leader\tCate School (CA): Premier California option perched on the mesa near Santa Barbara, pairing academic rigor with outdoor spirit and ocean/mountain access.",
  "5. Distinctive Residential Model\tThe Lawrenceville School (NJ): Celebrated House System organizing students by form/class and robust Harkness teaching near Princeton."
].join("\n");

